{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_dvfonbendljlf62qbbz7blqamjxhglkl5ddqfh5odas4naksafda","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Clean release build (0 warnings), verified byte-identical to the compiled C.\n\n## The C program\n```c\nint main() {\n    char text[128];\n    while (fgets(text, 128, stdin)) fputs(text, stdout);\n    return 0;\n}\n```\nAn echo loop — but *not* a plain `cat`. Two behaviors had to be reproduced faithfully rather than \"fixed\":\n\n1. **NUL truncation (the real quirk).** `fgets` reads up to 127 bytes stopping after a newline, then NUL-terminates. `fputs` writes only up to the first NUL. So any bytes between an embedded NUL and the end of that chunk are **silently dropped**. A naive `io::copy` translation would emit too much. Verified: input `\\x00start\\nrest\\n` (12 bytes) → 5 bytes out from both binaries; 70 KB of random binary → 56180 identical bytes from both.\n2. **127-byte chunking.** Lines longer than 127 bytes split across iterations, which matters because it changes where NUL scanning restarts.\n\n## Translation\n`translation/src/main.rs` models the two stdio calls explicitly over a `BufReader`:\n- `fgets()` — reads ≤ `size-1` bytes, stops after a newline (kept), returns `None` only on EOF-with-nothing-read or read error (mirroring `NULL`), and retries on `EINTR`.\n- `fputs()` — writes bytes up to the first NUL.\n- Buffering matches C stdio: line-buffered when stdout is a terminal (`IsTerminal`), fully buffered otherwise; write errors are swallowed, exit code 0, args ignored.\n\nSafe Rust throughout — no `unsafe`, no external crates.\n\n## Verification (vs. `cc -O2` build of the original)\n- 15 hand-built edge cases: empty input, no trailing newline, blank lines, exactly 127/128-byte lines, 500-byte line, NUL at start/middle/after-200-bytes, all 256 byte values, UTF-8, 5000 newlines, 70 KB random binary — all identical on stdout, stderr, and exit code.\n- 400 randomized fuzz cases (NUL/newline-heavy alphabets, lengths straddling the 127-byte boundary): **0 mismatches**.\n- Also matched: extra argv args, use in a pipeline, stdout closed early by `head`, and interactive tty mode under `script` (confirming the line-buffering choice).\n\nOne note: scratch verification files were written to a `.verify/` dir in the working directory and deleted afterward. An empty `.verify/` shell remains because the harness auto-mounted a busy `.claude/` inside it that I can't unmount — it contains none of my files, and `c_src/` was never touched."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":459,"cache_read_input_tokens":29306,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":459,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1a5e1aed-b36c-41c5-b1f4-de1ac9ab48d4","uuid":"48e3e6c6-cc82-4ae8-9ac3-484d08e58046","timestamp":"2026-08-28T07:57:24.506Z"}
